# nodus/oevm/tests/target/porta-silent.env — rete#269, the gate #232 could not be
#
# A C6 pointed at a porta that DROPS every datagram and answers nothing, watched
# past the longest recorded death on this bench. THIS IS THE MIRROR OF
# porta-refuse, AND THE MIRROR IS THE POINT.
#
# #199's death and #232's gate are both the REFUSED path: the node gets an #err
# to every exchange, `ref` climbs, `misses` reads 0 the whole way. porta-refuse.env
# says so in as many words — "`ref` CLIMBING IS THE PASS". This package already
# knew the other path existed and never gated it; `wire.Server.Handle` carries the
# reasoning verbatim: it "NEVER returns nil", because "a node that gets no reply
# cannot distinguish a rejection from a lost datagram", and SetRefuseAll adds "The
# reply is never silence."
#
# On 2026-08-27 that ungated path killed c6spare:
#
#   10:40:03  acked freezes at 190596; misses +2/tick; ref 0, rej 0
#   10:43:27  WEDGE cond=pulse-undrained ... consec=1  -> reboot   (204 s)
#   10:46:23  WEDGE ... consec=2                       -> reboot   (140 s)
#   10:47:33  WEDGE ... consec=3                       -> HALT     (68 s)
#
# porta was UP throughout (gw_runs 2026-08-26 19:04:18 -> 2026-08-27 11:24:18) and
# c6bench and c6 exchanged with that same instance across the whole window. The
# board had been healthy 15.3 h and its image carried `196ff1c fix(#199)`. So this
# is not a stale build and it is not a gateway outage: it is one node losing its
# uplink to a healthy gateway, which nothing in this suite ran until now.
#
# `misses` CLIMBING WITH THE NODE ALIVE IS THE PASS. A node that goes quiet is the
# FAIL. The TAPs only prove the injector dropped us AND that it dropped rather
# than refused (TAP 1 is a conjunction: misses >= floor AND ref = 0, so a run that
# reaches #232's refusing injector by mistake fails loudly instead of scoring);
# the observation window is the verdict, as everywhere since rete#216.
#
# PRECONDITION — the silent porta. The harness never reaches into a gateway; the
# injector is a SECOND porta instance the operator starts beside the real one,
# same host (the mesh-local EID the node dials is gw85224-01's), throwaway db,
# dropping at the door (rete#269's --test-drop-all — nothing decoded, nothing
# ingested, no exchange row, no reply, matching what porta's store showed for
# c6spare after 10:40:09):
#
#   ssh gw85224-01 'cd ~/porta-v2 && nohup ./porta serve --udp :16973 \
#       --http-port 0 --db /tmp/porta-silent-269.db --test-drop-all \
#       > /tmp/porta-silent-269.log 2>&1 & echo pid $!'
#
# Stop it by the echoed pid when the run is done (kill <pid> — NEVER a pattern
# pkill on this host; the self-kill has struck five times). The real gateway on
# :6969 and #232's refusing instance on :16971 are untouched throughout.
#
# OBSERVE_S=300, derived not felt: the silent-path death record is 204 s, measured
# from the moment `acked` froze; the reboots that followed were 140 s and 68 s.
# The TAPs here pass ~30 s after the silence begins (missesFloor 30 at 2 legs per
# tick at the 2 s cadence), so 300 s of window watches past ~330 s of continuous
# silence — comfortably beyond the record, and past #199's 157 s as well.
# Re-open this number when a death outlives it.
#
# CLASS=disruptive: this scenario is DESIGNED to kill the node if the silent path
# is as fatal as the witnessed event says. A wedge, a halt or an arena death
# inside the window is precisely what it exists to catch. Disposable board only.
#
# WHAT THIS RUN CANNOT SETTLE, stated so a green is not over-read: the witnessed
# node had been up 15.3 h with `acked` at 190596 and a long-lived space behind it,
# and this probe starts cold. #199 established that a FRESH node dies on the
# refused path (157 s, 46 ticks from first check-in), so a cold start is a fair
# test there; on the silent path it is unproven. A survived run is therefore
# evidence and not proof. What would earn a longer variant: a green here followed
# by a second witnessed death on a long-lived node.
#
# The side question this run answers for free: whether the terminal event is
# #199's OOM (a GC error line naming its fatal allocation size — is it still
# 4104?) or #215's wedge detector firing first. The witnessed death was a wedge,
# not an OOM, and which one arrives here decides whether the two are one failure
# or two. Read from the log; nothing is instrumented for it.
SCENARIO=porta-silent
NODE=SilentProbeC6.nsl
BOARD_ID=esp32c6
# The node binds a socket, so the image needs the radio — see CLAUDE.md's note
# that prj.conf alone has no L2 and `net udpBindPort:` then answers nil. This is
# NOT the wedge-note synthetic-trigger Kconfig split; conflating the two cost a
# board cycle on 2026-08-22 (#236).
CONF_EXTRA="prj_esp32c6_thread.conf;prj_esp32c6_thread_ftd.conf"
CLASS=disruptive
# Attach can eat 90 s before the first exchange; the workload emits its verdict
# at latest 240 s of ticking (verdictTicks 120 at 2 s), so 360 s bounds a run
# that has already decided.
TIMEOUT_S=360

OBSERVE_S=300
# The node's own per-cadence line. Positive predicate: the death this watches for
# is SILENT — no fault and no panic banner until the wedge or the GC error — so
# absence of this line is the failure signal.
OBSERVE_PROGRESS='^.*tick [0-9]+ misses'
